# This repo builds a Linux OCI image. Every committed file is consumed
# on Linux (shell scripts, systemd units, sysctl/tmpfiles confs, YAML
# recipes, .just files). CRLF leaking in from a Windows checkout will
# silently break bash (`\r` in args), tmpfiles.d parsing, and more.
#
# Normalize to LF on commit and force LF on checkout, regardless of the
# committer's platform or core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files — never line-end-normalize even if git's auto-detection
# guesses wrong.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
*.gz      binary
*.tar     binary
*.tgz     binary
*.zip     binary
*.key     binary
*.private binary
